=20

Hi,
=20
Is there a command/tool that will allow you to move the contents of a
disk to another disk while the data is online. Sorry to compare UNIX's
but I know in AIX you can "mirgatepv" where you add a disk to a Logical
Volume (domain) and then you can just migrate the data to the new disk
then remove the old disk, all with out an outage.
Now I looked at the "migrate" command but that looks like one file at a
time thing. Any ideas ??
=20
Thanks in advance,
Adrian

