=20
Thanks to all that helped, I was amazed at the good & speedy responces.
I won't mention any names due to privacy.

The answer is yes.  If your files systems are AdvFS and if you have the
AdvFS Utilities License.  Your data is in domains already and all you
have to do is add one disk of equal or greater size to the domain and
then withdraw the old disk and the data will migrate automatically
without operational interruption.
Other conventional options was like a tar or vdump piped to vrestore
which requires an outage.

Thanks for your help to everyone involved.
Adrian





