A. Direct login on the terminal server using, connecting to a specific 
port using a defined service protected by a password (NOT
ENCRYPTED, optional terminal server access password)
                                                                                                                                                             
B. Connecting by telnet to a service assigned to a serial port (no 
additional access control - e.g. not even a password, use IP
security table if available!)
                                                                                                                                                             
C. Direct connecting by LAT (depreciated, proprietary protocol, but 
alloes a service password)



