There has been one response (thanks Iain) to my question regarding a
loopback filesystem / disk driver for Tru64 UNIX (formerly Digital UNIX):

There are two similar (and unsupported) ``loopback disk drivers'', but
unfortunately non of them works fully on 4.0G:

  - The ldisk driver, which worked for me on 4.0D seems to partially fail on
    4.0G (mounting a device associated with an iso image file fails).

    It seems that the source for this driver got lost within HP...

  - The dkless driver:  ``The dkless module enables Digital Unix to page to
    a file.  The dkless support provides a block mode device which is
    associated, by the user, to a filepath.''  (From the dkless
    configuration instructions.)

    I received a copy of this (also unsupported) driver for Tru64 5.1A/B.

Regards,

	\franz

